diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/README.md b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..fb7245290b3d556698f18d82329a71aedeb3fb77
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# Menu tree UI
+
+Experimental, scalable replacement for core's `menu_ui` admin form, designed to
+handle menus with thousands of links without falling over.
+
+This is an experimental core module. It coexists with `menu_ui`: enabling it makes
+the tree the primary **Edit links** action and the "Links" tab for each menu (under
+Administration » Structure » Menus), and demotes `menu_ui`'s classic tabledrag
+overview to an "Edit links (no js)" action and a "Links (no js)" tab alongside it.
+The classic UI stays available as the no-JS fallback while this module matures.
+
+## What works
+
+- Lazy-loaded tree: only the top level loads on page open; each subtree fetches on expand.
+- Browser-native row virtualization via `content-visibility: auto`, plus an `IntersectionObserver` fallback that flips deep off-screen rows to `visibility: hidden` with a reserved height.
+- Full WAI-ARIA tree keyboard navigation (Up/Down/Left/Right/Home/End/Enter, roving `tabindex`).
+- Pointer drag-and-drop reorder and re-parent, plus two keyboard equivalents: Shift+Up / Shift+Down for a quick sibling reorder, and a grab/select move mode (Space to pick up, arrows to choose a before/after/child position, Enter to drop, Escape to cancel) that steps through the same drop-intent space as drag and commits through the same path.
+- A "Keyboard commands" dialog, linked at the top of the page so assistive-technology users meet it early.
+- htmx-driven search panel returning HTML partials, with jump-to-result.
+- Edits delegated to core's existing per-link form.
+- Save / Cancel working copy: reorders (drag and keyboard) are recorded in a
+  per-user shared tempstore rather than written immediately, and the tree
+  overlays them so unsaved changes are visible. **Save** replays the recorded
+  moves to storage; **Cancel** discards them. A second editor of the same menu
+  sees a lock notice and cannot save over the first. Column toggles (e.g.
+  "Enabled") and the per-row Edit/Delete forms still commit immediately —
+  the working copy covers reorder structure only.
+
+## Architecture
+
+Menu tree UI is a **consumer** of two generic experimental modules that were
+extracted from it:
+
+- **Tree grid** (`treegrid`) — the reusable spine: the `<drupal-treegrid>`
+  custom element, one-level-at-a-time lazy loading, row windowing, WAI-ARIA
+  keyboard navigation with a roving `tabindex`, and a column-plugin system with
+  a client-side cell-renderer registry.
+- **Tree grid reorder** (`treegrid_reorder`) — the drag-and-drop and keyboard
+  reordering layer: gesture handling, universal move validation (a node cannot
+  be dropped onto itself or into one of its own descendants), and the per-user
+  Save/Cancel working copy.
+
+Menu tree UI supplies the menu-specific pieces on top: the row renderer, the
+`Enabled` / `Operations` column plugins, the move handler (which
+links may move, the 9-level depth cap, and the write through the menu link
+manager), and the routes below.
+
+Routes, by intent:
+
+| Route | Returns | Used by |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree` | Full HTML page with top level rendered | Direct browser visit (the "Edit links" operation / "Links" tab on a menu) |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/children?parent={id}` | JSON `{ parent, items[] }` | `<drupal-treegrid>` element on expand |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/search?q=…` | HTML fragment | htmx swap from the search input |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/move` | JSON `{ ok, … }` | Drag/keyboard reorder — records to the working copy (POST) |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/column-update` | JSON `{ ok, … }` | Column switch toggle (POST) |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/save` | JSON `{ ok, … }` | Commit the working copy's moves to storage (POST) |
+| `/admin/structure/menu/manage/{menu}/tree/cancel` | JSON `{ ok }` | Discard the working copy (POST) |
+
+`MenuTreeLoader::loadLevel()` wraps `MenuLinkTreeInterface::load()` with
+`MenuTreeParameters::setRoot()->excludeRoot()->setMaxDepth(1)` to fetch exactly one
+level — never the whole menu.
+
+### JavaScript
+
+The frontend is hand-authored, no-build classic JavaScript, matching core's
+convention (no bundler, no TypeScript, no ESM).
+
+The interactive element is `<drupal-treegrid>`, defined by the `treegrid`
+module — not by this one. Its `connectedCallback` fires automatically when the
+element enters the DOM (including htmx-swapped content), and it exposes
+lifecycle events (`treegrid:connected` / `treegrid:disconnect`) and an
+interaction-handler registry (`addClickHandler` / `addKeyHandler`). Menu tree UI
+attaches its own features to those hooks.
+
+Generic behavior lives in the two upstream modules, under the `Drupal.treegrid`
+and `Drupal.treegridReorder` namespaces:
+
+- `treegrid/js/` — `treegrid-element.js` (the custom element), `tree-nav.js`
+  (row walking + roving-tabindex focus), `expand.js` (lazy load + collapse,
+  `ExpandManager`), `windowing.js` (`IntersectionObserver` virtualization,
+  `RowWindow`), `keyboard.js` (WAI-ARIA navigation keys), `cells.js` (the
+  cell-renderer registry).
+- `treegrid_reorder/js/` — `controller.js` / `intent.js` / `indicator.js` /
+  `commit.js` (pointer drag), `move-mode.js` (keyboard grab/select), and
+  `reorder-keys.js` (Shift+Arrow). These are parameterized by a config object
+  so they carry no menu CSS knowledge of their own.
+
+Menu tree UI's own JavaScript is a `Drupal.behaviors` attach (the element itself
+is generic), under the `Drupal.menuTreeUi` namespace:
+
+- `js/menu-tree.js` — the behaviors entry point: on each upgraded element, wires
+  reorder, the column controls, search jump-to, and the keyboard-help dialog
+  through the element's events and interaction registry.
+- `js/row-builder.js` — turns the children JSON into row DOM (`buildRow` /
+  `buildRows`) and registers the menu row renderer as a `<drupal-treegrid>`
+  provider.
+- `js/search.js` — the htmx search panel behavior.
+- `js/jump-to.js` — document-level jump-from-search-result.
+- `js/working-copy.js` — the Save / Cancel action bar.
+
+The element upgrades the server-rendered top level (from
+`templates/menu-tree-ui-page.html.twig`) rather than rebuilding from scratch:
+
+- First paint is the real tree, not a loading spinner.
+- No-JS users see at least the top level.
+- Row markup for children built in JS mirrors
+  `templates/menu-tree-ui-row.html.twig`, and the cell widgets mirror the
+  renderers in `treegrid/js/cells.js`. They must be kept in sync — see the
+  `NB:` comment in `js/row-builder.js`.
+
+## Constraints inherited from core
+
+- **9-level depth cap.** `menu_tree.p1`–`p9` is the materialized path columns in core. Links deeper than 9 don't work in Drupal at all — not specific to this module.
+
+## Generating a test dataset
+
+The `menu_tree_ui_test` submodule (under `tests/modules/`) ships a Drush
+command for seeding and purging large test menus (handy for manually
+exercising the UI at scale; not for production). It requires Drush to be
+installed in your environment.
+
+Because it is a test module, it is not discovered on a normal site. To enable
+it on a development site, allow test extensions to be scanned first — add to
+`settings.php` (or `settings.local.php`):
+
+```php
+$settings['extension_discovery_scan_tests'] = TRUE;
+```
+
+```bash
+drush en menu_tree_ui_test
+drush mtu:seed main                          # default: 5 levels, 15,045 links, lorem titles
+drush mtu:seed main --counts=10,10,10,10,10  # balanced 5-level tree (111,110 links)
+drush mtu:seed main --counts=5000            # wide single-level stress test
+drush mtu:seed main --seed=42 --dry-run      # reproducible run, plan only
+```
+
+Cleaning up — by default only deletes links the seeder created (titles starting
+with `mtu`):
+
+```bash
+drush mtu:purge main
+drush mtu:purge main --prefix=""             # nuke ALL menu_link_content links — careful
+```
+
+The seeder batches saves and resets entity storage statics every 500 writes to
+keep peak memory bounded.
+
+## Why the duplication between Twig and JS row rendering?
+
+`templates/menu-tree-ui-row.html.twig` renders the initial top level.
+`js/row-builder.js` renders children fetched at runtime. They produce identical DOM
+from different sources.
+
+The alternative — returning HTML partials from the children endpoint instead of
+JSON — was rejected because the client needs the structured data for drag-and-drop,
+optimistic updates, and ordering arithmetic. Building that on top of an
+HTML-partial endpoint is harder than living with a small render duplication.
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/css/menu-tree-ui.css b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/css/menu-tree-ui.css
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..39725e735b94ebae25b072b0aa2c3b27e4c1e13f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/css/menu-tree-ui.css
@@ -0,0 +1,499 @@
+/*
+ * Menu tree UI styles.
+ *
+ * Strategy: define a thin bridge layer of --mtu-color-* variables, scoped to
+ * .menu-tree-ui. All color rules in this file use ONLY those bridge
+ * variables — never hardcoded hex. Each bridge variable resolves to a
+ * semantic token of the default admin theme (--admin-color-*, dark-mode
+ * aware via light-dark()) with a static light-scheme fallback for themes
+ * that do not define the token. Any theme can also override the bridge
+ * variables on its own selectors.
+ *
+ * Virtualization: [data-virtualized="true"] is set by RowWindow
+ * (IntersectionObserver, see treegrid/js/windowing.js) for rows deep
+ * off-screen; the rule below hard-floors their cost via visibility:hidden +
+ * fixed height.
+ */
+
+.menu-tree-ui {
+  --mtu-color-divider: var(--admin-color-border, #e0e0e0);
+  --mtu-color-divider-light: var(--admin-color-border-table, #f0f0f0);
+  --mtu-color-bg: var(--admin-color-bg-surface, #fff);
+  --mtu-color-bg-raised: var(--admin-color-bg-raised, #fff);
+  --mtu-color-bg-inset: var(--admin-color-bg-sunken, #f0f0f0);
+  --mtu-color-text: var(--admin-color-text, #1a1a1a);
+  --mtu-color-text-muted: var(--admin-color-text-soft, #757575);
+  --mtu-color-icon: var(--admin-color-icon, #787878);
+  --mtu-color-focus: var(--admin-color-focus, #2563eb);
+  --mtu-color-link: var(--admin-color-link, #2563eb);
+  --mtu-color-focus-bg: var(--admin-color-bg-item, rgb(37, 99, 235, 0.08));
+  --mtu-shadow-popover: var(--admin-shadow-2, 0 8px 24px rgb(0, 0, 0, 0.12));
+
+  display: flex;
+  flex-direction: column;
+  gap: 1rem;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The search container anchors the results popover. `position: relative`
+ * scopes the absolutely-positioned results below.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__search-container {
+  position: relative;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The search <input> carries the `form-element` class so the admin theme
+ * supplies its padding, border, border-radius, and font — no overrides needed here.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__search-input {
+  width: 100%;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Autocomplete-style results popover. Hangs from the input on its z-axis.
+ * `:not(:has(*))` hides it when the htmx swap leaves no element children.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__search-results {
+  position: absolute;
+  z-index: 10;
+  top: calc(100% + 0.25rem);
+  right: 0;
+  left: 0;
+  overflow-y: auto;
+  max-height: 60vh;
+  padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
+  border: 1px solid var(--mtu-color-divider);
+  border-radius: 4px;
+  background: var(--mtu-color-bg-raised);
+  box-shadow: var(--mtu-shadow-popover);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__search-results:not(:has(*)) {
+  display: none;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__empty,
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__summary {
+  margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text-muted);
+  font-size: 0.85rem;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__list {
+  margin: 0;
+  padding: 0;
+  list-style: none;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__item {
+  padding: 0.5rem 0;
+  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--mtu-color-divider-light);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__item:last-child {
+  border-bottom: 0;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__title {
+  display: inline-block;
+  padding: 0;
+  cursor: pointer;
+  text-align: left;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-link);
+  border: 0;
+  background: transparent;
+  font: inherit;
+  font-weight: 600;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__title:hover,
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__title:focus {
+  text-decoration: underline;
+  outline: none;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__title:focus-visible {
+  outline: 2px solid var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  outline-offset: 2px;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__breadcrumb {
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text-muted);
+  font-size: 0.8rem;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-search-results__item--disabled .menu-tree-ui-search-results__title {
+  text-decoration: line-through;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text-muted);
+}
+
+/* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── save / cancel */
+
+/*
+ * The action bar sticks to the top while the tree scrolls (the column header
+ * is intentionally not sticky). wrap-reverse keeps Save/Cancel on the left with
+ * the unsaved notice pushed to their right, and sends the notice to a line
+ * ABOVE the buttons (not below) once the row is too narrow. A solid background
+ * keeps scrolled rows from showing through; the z-index sits above the rows but
+ * below the search results popover (z-index 10).
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__action-bar {
+  position: sticky;
+  z-index: 4;
+  top: 0;
+  display: flex;
+  flex-wrap: wrap-reverse;
+  align-items: center;
+  gap: 0.5rem 1rem;
+  padding-block: 0.5rem;
+  background: var(--mtu-color-bg);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__actions {
+  display: flex;
+  align-items: center;
+  gap: 0.75rem;
+}
+
+/*
+ * The unsaved notice rides in the action bar rather than the message space:
+ * sized to its content and pushed to the right edge when it shares the row with
+ * the buttons (wrap-reverse lifts it above them when it cannot fit). Its
+ * vertical padding is trimmed to the Save/Cancel row height so revealing it does
+ * not grow the sticky bar and shift the tree below it; the descendant selector
+ * outranks the themed .messages padding it would otherwise inherit.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__action-bar .menu-tree-ui__unsaved {
+  flex: 0 1 auto;
+  margin: 0;
+  margin-inline-start: auto;
+  padding-block: 0.25rem;
+}
+
+/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── tree */
+
+/*
+ * The tree is a real <table>, so the admin theme styles the header, cell
+ * padding, borders, and row hover for free — matching the classic menu admin.
+ * Only the tree-specific bits below are layered on top.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__table {
+  width: 100%;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__table td {
+  vertical-align: middle;
+}
+
+/* The checkbox column controls sit centered under their header. The
+   operations column is a full column too, but its dropbutton keeps the default
+   alignment. */
+.menu-tree-ui__col--data,
+.menu-tree-ui-row__column:not([data-column="operations"]) {
+  text-align: center;
+}
+
+/* The operations dropbutton is a list; drop the theme's bullets and margins. */
+.menu-tree-ui-row__operations li,
+.menu-tree-ui-row__operations ul {
+  margin: 0;
+  padding: 0;
+  list-style: none;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Keep the keyboard cursor clear of the sticky action bar. focusRow() lets the
+ * browser scroll a focused row into view, and the browser ignores the sticky
+ * overlay, so without this the cursor can land hidden under the bar. The offset
+ * is the bar's live height: menu-tree.js measures it into --mtu-sticky-offset
+ * and keeps it current as the bar wraps; the fallback covers the moment before
+ * that script runs.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row {
+  scroll-margin-block-start: var(--mtu-sticky-offset, 4rem);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Highlight the row that holds focus (on its handle, toggle, switch, or links).
+ * Raise it above its neighbors so the focused control's focus ring — which the
+ * theme draws as a box-shadow extending outside the element — is not painted
+ * over by the adjacent rows.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row:focus-within {
+  position: relative;
+  z-index: 1;
+  background-color: var(--mtu-color-focus-bg);
+}
+
+@keyframes menu-tree-ui-flash {
+  0% {
+    background-color: var(--mtu-color-focus-bg);
+  }
+  100% {
+    background-color: transparent;
+  }
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row--flash {
+  animation: menu-tree-ui-flash 1.2s ease-out;
+}
+
+@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
+  .menu-tree-ui-row--flash {
+    animation: none;
+    background-color: var(--mtu-color-focus-bg);
+  }
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__name {
+  display: flex;
+  align-items: center;
+  gap: 0.5rem;
+  min-width: 0;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle {
+  display: inline-flex;
+  align-items: center;
+  justify-content: center;
+  width: 1.875rem;
+  height: 2.25rem;
+  cursor: grab;
+  user-select: none;
+  touch-action: none;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-icon);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Movable handles reuse core's tabledrag move icon so the affordance matches
+ * the classic menu admin. The icon is a mask filled with currentColor, so it
+ * follows the handle's color in both color schemes and picks up the
+ * stronger text color on hover/focus. The locked variant overrides this
+ * back to a dimmed dot below.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle-icon {
+  display: inline-block;
+  width: 14px;
+  height: 14px;
+  background-color: currentColor;
+  font-size: 0;
+  mask-image: url(../../../misc/icons/787878/move.svg);
+  mask-repeat: no-repeat;
+  mask-position: center;
+  mask-size: contain;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle:hover,
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle:focus-visible {
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle:focus-visible {
+  outline: 2px solid var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  outline-offset: -2px;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle--locked {
+  cursor: default;
+  opacity: 0.3;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__handle--locked .menu-tree-ui-row__handle-icon {
+  width: auto;
+  height: auto;
+  background-color: transparent;
+  font-size: 0.6rem;
+  mask-image: none;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row--dragging {
+  opacity: 0.4;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row--dragging .menu-tree-ui-row__handle {
+  cursor: grabbing;
+}
+
+/* Pointer drop-as-child target. */
+.menu-tree-ui-row--drop-as-child {
+  outline: 2px solid var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  outline-offset: -2px;
+  background-color: var(--mtu-color-focus-bg);
+}
+
+/*
+ * The row currently picked up in keyboard move mode. Dashed (vs the solid
+ * drop-as-child target outline) reads as "in hand, not yet placed".
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row--grabbed {
+  outline: 2px dashed var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  outline-offset: -2px;
+  background-color: var(--mtu-color-focus-bg);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-drop-indicator {
+  position: absolute;
+  z-index: 5;
+  display: none;
+  height: 3px;
+  margin-top: -1.5px;
+  pointer-events: none;
+  border-radius: 1.5px;
+  background: var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  box-shadow: -3px 0 0 var(--mtu-color-focus);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__toggle {
+  display: inline-flex;
+  align-items: center;
+  justify-content: center;
+  width: 2rem;
+  height: 2rem;
+  padding: 0;
+  cursor: pointer;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text);
+  border: 0;
+  background: transparent;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__toggle--spacer {
+  cursor: default;
+}
+
+/*
+ * CSS-drawn chevron (font-size:0 hides the ▸ glyph; borders form the arrow).
+ * Collapsed: rotate(45deg) → right.  Expanded: rotate(135deg) → down.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row__chevron {
+  display: inline-block;
+  width: 0.5rem;
+  height: 0.5rem;
+  transition: transform 160ms ease;
+  transform: rotate(45deg);
+  transform-origin: 50% 50%;
+  border-top: 0.125rem solid currentColor;
+  border-right: 0.125rem solid currentColor;
+  font-size: 0;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row[aria-expanded="true"] .menu-tree-ui-row__chevron {
+  transform: rotate(135deg);
+}
+
+@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
+  .menu-tree-ui-row__chevron {
+    transition: none;
+  }
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__title {
+  overflow: hidden;
+  flex: 1 1 auto;
+  min-width: 0;
+  white-space: nowrap;
+  text-overflow: ellipsis;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row--disabled .menu-tree-ui-row__title {
+  text-decoration: line-through;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text-muted);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Hard-floor virtualization: rows deep off-screen hide their content but
+ * keep their height so the scrollbar stays accurate.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui-row[data-virtualized="true"] > .menu-tree-ui-row__cell {
+  visibility: hidden;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row[data-virtualized="true"] {
+  height: 2.5rem;
+}
+
+/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── operations */
+
+.menu-tree-ui-row__operations {
+  flex: 0 0 auto;
+  margin-inline-start: auto;
+}
+
+/* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── keyboard help */
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-toggle {
+  align-self: flex-start;
+  padding: 0;
+  cursor: pointer;
+  text-decoration: underline;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-link);
+  border: 0;
+  background: transparent;
+  font: inherit;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-toggle:focus-visible {
+  outline: 2px solid var(--mtu-color-focus);
+  outline-offset: 2px;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog {
+  width: calc(100% - 2rem);
+  max-width: 32rem;
+  padding: 0;
+  color: var(--mtu-color-text);
+  border: 1px solid var(--mtu-color-divider);
+  border-radius: 6px;
+  background: var(--mtu-color-bg);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog::backdrop {
+  background: rgb(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog-inner {
+  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog h2 {
+  margin-top: 0;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-list {
+  display: grid;
+  grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
+  gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
+  margin: 0 0 1rem;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-list dt {
+  white-space: nowrap;
+  font-weight: 600;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-list dd {
+  margin: 0;
+}
+
+.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog kbd {
+  display: inline-block;
+  padding: 0.05rem 0.35rem;
+  border: 1px solid var(--mtu-color-divider);
+  border-radius: 3px;
+  background: var(--mtu-color-bg-inset);
+  font-size: 0.85em;
+}
+
+/* "Add link" primary action, above the search box. */
+.menu-tree-ui__primary-actions {
+  margin-block-end: 1rem;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Scroll sentinel for top-level paging: an empty, non-interactive marker after
+ * the table. A small height keeps the IntersectionObserver reliable across
+ * browsers.
+ */
+.menu-tree-ui__paging-sentinel {
+  height: 1px;
+}
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/jump-to.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/jump-to.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d8b8146f0eea7bdecb43e1be6dfc309857b06cd8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/jump-to.js
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Jump-to from a search result.
+ *
+ * Search results live in the htmx-injected sidebar, outside <drupal-treegrid>. The
+ * listener attaches at document level so it works across swaps.
+ *
+ * Exposes Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachJumpClickHandler.
+ */
+
+((Drupal) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+  const { findRow, focusRow } = Drupal.treegrid.treeNav;
+
+  const FLASH_MS = 1200;
+
+  /**
+   * Walks the ancestor chain (root-to-parent), expanding each level (lazy-
+   * loading its children if needed), then scrolls and focuses the target.
+   *
+   * @param {object} ctx
+   *   Context: {tree: HTMLTableElement, expand: ExpandManager, moveMode?:
+   *   MoveModeController}.
+   * @param {string} targetId
+   *   The link plugin ID to jump to.
+   * @param {string[]} pathIds
+   *   Ancestor IDs from root to parent.
+   *
+   * @return {Promise<void>}
+   *   Resolves once the jump completes (or aborts).
+   */
+  async function jumpTo(ctx, targetId, pathIds) {
+    // Sequential expansion: each level must be open before the next is in DOM.
+    // eslint-disable-next-line no-restricted-syntax
+    for (const ancestorId of pathIds) {
+      const row = findRow(ctx.tree, ancestorId);
+      if (!row) {
+        // eslint-disable-next-line no-console
+        console.warn(
+          '[menu-tree] jump aborted: ancestor not in DOM',
+          ancestorId,
+        );
+        return;
+      }
+      if (row.getAttribute('aria-expanded') !== 'true') {
+        // eslint-disable-next-line no-await-in-loop
+        await ctx.expand.expand(row);
+      }
+    }
+    const target = findRow(ctx.tree, targetId);
+    if (!target) {
+      // eslint-disable-next-line no-console
+      console.warn(
+        '[menu-tree] jump target not found after expansion',
+        targetId,
+      );
+      return;
+    }
+    target.scrollIntoView({ block: 'center', behavior: 'smooth' });
+    // If a move is in progress, the editor searched for a destination: keep the
+    // grab and re-aim the cursor at the jumped-to row instead of stealing focus.
+    if (ctx.moveMode?.isActive()) {
+      ctx.moveMode.aimAt(target);
+    } else {
+      focusRow(ctx.tree, target);
+    }
+    target.classList.add('menu-tree-ui-row--flash');
+    window.setTimeout(() => {
+      target.classList.remove('menu-tree-ui-row--flash');
+    }, FLASH_MS);
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Wires document-level click handling for [data-mtu-jump-id].
+   *
+   * @param {object} ctx
+   *   Context: {tree: HTMLTableElement, expand: ExpandManager}.
+   *
+   * @return {function(MouseEvent): void}
+   *   The bound handler, so the caller can remove it on teardown.
+   */
+  function attachJumpClickHandler(ctx) {
+    const handler = (event) => {
+      const { target } = event;
+      if (!(target instanceof Element)) {
+        return;
+      }
+      const trigger = target.closest('[data-mtu-jump-id]');
+      if (!trigger) {
+        return;
+      }
+      const targetId = trigger.dataset.mtuJumpId;
+      if (!targetId) {
+        return;
+      }
+      event.preventDefault();
+      const pathAttr = trigger.dataset.mtuJumpPath ?? '';
+      const path = pathAttr === '' ? [] : pathAttr.split(',');
+      jumpTo(ctx, targetId, path);
+    };
+    document.addEventListener('click', handler);
+    return handler;
+  }
+
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachJumpClickHandler = attachJumpClickHandler;
+})(Drupal);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/menu-tree.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/menu-tree.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..ebb2b3e665644c30e8405e0cf9af7cc7fe575296
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/menu-tree.js
@@ -0,0 +1,420 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * menu_tree_ui's features for <drupal-treegrid>.
+ *
+ * The treegrid spine — lazy expand, row windowing, WAI-ARIA navigation, and the
+ * roving-tabindex focus model — lives in the treegrid module's <drupal-treegrid>
+ * element. The menu row renderer is registered as a provider in row-builder.js.
+ * This file wires the menu-specific features onto an upgraded element:
+ *  - reorder: pointer drag, the keyboard grab/select move mode, Shift+Arrow
+ *    sibling reorder, and the single-pointer commit (tap the handle);
+ *  - the column switches;
+ *  - search jump-to and dismiss;
+ *  - the "Keyboard commands" dialog.
+ *
+ * Features attach through the element's interaction-handler registry
+ * (addClickHandler / addKeyHandler) and its lifecycle. The handlers run ahead of
+ * the element's built-in navigation and return true to consume an event, which
+ * preserves the original dispatch order (move mode, then columns, then nav).
+ */
+
+((Drupal, drupalSettings, once) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+  const ns = Drupal.menuTreeUi;
+  const rr = Drupal.treegridReorder;
+  const { rowOf, childRows, descendantRows } = Drupal.treegrid.treeNav;
+  const { announce } = Drupal.treegrid;
+
+  const ROW = 'tr[role="row"]';
+  const COLUMN_TOGGLE = '.treegrid-cell-checkbox';
+  // Elements that must keep their native/authored key behavior instead of the
+  // row's, e.g. Enter on the title link or Space on the Enabled checkbox. The
+  // expand toggle is exempted: it is a <button> that legitimately takes focus
+  // on mouse click and must keep responding to Enter/Space.
+  const INTERACTIVE = 'a, button, input, select, textarea';
+
+  /**
+   * Syncs a parent row's "parent or leaf" attributes to its current children.
+   *
+   * The treegrid_reorder commit pipeline calls this (as a configured callback)
+   * after a move refresh: /children?parent=X returns X's children, not X's own
+   * metadata, so this is the one piece of state derived client-side. It is
+   * menu-specific — it rebuilds the disclosure toggle and reads menu row markup
+   * — so it stays here rather than in the generic module. Skipped when parentId
+   * is '' (root has no enclosing row) or the row isn't in the DOM.
+   *
+   * @param {string} parentId
+   *   The parent plugin ID.
+   */
+  function applyParentMetadata(parentId) {
+    if (parentId === '') {
+      return;
+    }
+    const row = document.querySelector(
+      `${ROW}[data-id="${CSS.escape(parentId)}"]`,
+    );
+    if (!row) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const hasChildrenNow = childRows(row).length > 0;
+    row.dataset.hasChildren = hasChildrenNow ? 'true' : 'false';
+
+    const name = row.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui-row__name');
+    if (!name) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const existing = name.querySelector(':scope > .menu-tree-ui-row__toggle');
+
+    if (hasChildrenNow) {
+      row.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
+      if (!existing || existing.tagName.toLowerCase() !== 'button') {
+        const title =
+          name.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui-row__title')?.textContent?.trim() ??
+          '';
+        const button = ns.buildToggle({ has_children: true, title });
+        if (existing) {
+          existing.replaceWith(button);
+        } else {
+          name.prepend(button);
+        }
+      }
+    } else {
+      row.removeAttribute('aria-expanded');
+      if (existing && existing.tagName.toLowerCase() === 'button') {
+        existing.replaceWith(ns.buildToggle({ has_children: false }));
+      }
+      // On becoming a leaf, remove any stale descendant rows left behind,
+      // unobserving each so the row window does not retain detached nodes.
+      const rowWindow = row.closest('drupal-treegrid')?.rowWindow;
+      descendantRows(row).forEach((r) => {
+        rowWindow?.unobserve(r);
+        r.remove();
+      });
+      delete row.dataset.loaded;
+    }
+  }
+
+  // The menu's CSS class/selector names and commit callbacks, handed to the
+  // generic treegrid_reorder controllers so they carry no menu markup knowledge.
+  const REORDER_CONFIG = {
+    handleSelector: '.menu-tree-ui-row__handle',
+    lockedClass: 'menu-tree-ui-row__handle--locked',
+    draggingClass: 'menu-tree-ui-row--dragging',
+    grabbedClass: 'menu-tree-ui-row--grabbed',
+    lineClass: 'menu-tree-ui-drop-indicator',
+    dropAsChildClass: 'menu-tree-ui-row--drop-as-child',
+    titleSelector: '.menu-tree-ui-row__title',
+    rowControlsSelector:
+      '.menu-tree-ui-row__toggle, .menu-tree-ui-row__column, .menu-tree-ui-row__operations',
+    flashClass: 'menu-tree-ui-row--flash',
+    applyParentMetadata,
+    // Tell the working-copy action bar a change was recorded so it can reveal
+    // the unsaved notice (the bar lives outside the <drupal-treegrid> element).
+    onCommitted: () =>
+      document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('menu-tree-ui:changed')),
+  };
+
+  /**
+   * Persists a column checkbox change, reverting it if the server rejects it.
+   *
+   * The click is not prevented, so the browser has already flipped the checkbox
+   * by the time this runs; the new value is read from .checked and only rolled
+   * back on failure.
+   *
+   * @param {HTMLInputElement} checkbox
+   *   The toggled checkbox.
+   * @param {string} url
+   *   The column-update endpoint.
+   * @param {function(): (string|undefined)} getToken
+   *   Returns the current CSRF token.
+   *
+   * @return {Promise<void>}
+   *   Resolves once the update round-trips (or is reverted).
+   */
+  async function handleColumnToggle(checkbox, url, getToken) {
+    if (!url) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const { columnId, linkId } = checkbox.dataset;
+    if (!columnId || !linkId) {
+      return;
+    }
+
+    const newValue = checkbox.checked;
+
+    try {
+      const response = await fetch(url, {
+        method: 'POST',
+        headers: {
+          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
+          'X-CSRF-Token': getToken() ?? '',
+        },
+        credentials: 'same-origin',
+        body: JSON.stringify({
+          column_id: columnId,
+          link_id: linkId,
+          value: newValue,
+        }),
+      });
+      const data = await response.json();
+      if (!data.ok) {
+        checkbox.checked = !newValue;
+        announce(data.message ?? Drupal.t('Update failed.'), 'assertive');
+      }
+    } catch (e) {
+      checkbox.checked = !newValue;
+      announce(Drupal.t('Update failed.'), 'assertive');
+    }
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Wires menu_tree_ui's features onto an upgraded <drupal-treegrid>.
+   *
+   * @param {HTMLElement} element
+   *   The element, already connected (element.tree / element.expand are set).
+   */
+  function wireFeatures(element) {
+    if (!element.expand) {
+      // The element has not finished initializing yet (its provider can
+      // register after this behavior runs). Wire once it announces it is ready
+      // via treegrid:connected, rather than silently doing nothing.
+      element.addEventListener(
+        'treegrid:connected',
+        () => wireFeatures(element),
+        { once: true },
+      );
+      return;
+    }
+    const { tree, expand } = element;
+    const settings = drupalSettings.menuTreeUi ?? {};
+    const { moveUrl, columnUpdateUrl } = settings;
+    const container = element.closest('.menu-tree-ui');
+
+    // Keep the keyboard cursor clear of the sticky action bar: when focusRow()
+    // scrolls a focused row into view the browser ignores the sticky overlay,
+    // so the rows' scroll-margin (see CSS) must match the bar's height. The bar
+    // grows when the unsaved notice wraps above the buttons, so track it live.
+    const actionBar = container?.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__action-bar');
+    let stickyObserver = null;
+    if (actionBar && container && 'ResizeObserver' in window) {
+      const syncStickyOffset = () =>
+        container.style.setProperty(
+          '--mtu-sticky-offset',
+          `${actionBar.offsetHeight}px`,
+        );
+      syncStickyOffset();
+      stickyObserver = new ResizeObserver(syncStickyOffset);
+      stickyObserver.observe(actionBar);
+    }
+
+    let csrfToken;
+    let drag = null;
+    const getToken = () => csrfToken;
+
+    // One drop indicator, shared by pointer drag and keyboard move mode so the
+    // two never render into separate live regions. The host owns its position.
+    const indicator = new rr.DropIndicator(element, REORDER_CONFIG);
+    const moveMode = moveUrl
+      ? new rr.MoveModeController(
+          tree,
+          moveUrl,
+          expand,
+          indicator,
+          getToken,
+          REORDER_CONFIG,
+        )
+      : null;
+
+    /**
+     * Handles a tap (mouse, no drag) on a row's drag handle.
+     *
+     * Idle: picks the row up (the single-pointer counterpart to Space). During a
+     * move: tapping the carried item's handle drops it (the single-pointer
+     * commit, WCAG 2.5.7); taps on other rows' handles are ignored.
+     *
+     * @param {HTMLElement} row
+     *   The row whose handle was tapped.
+     */
+    const onHandleTap = (row) => {
+      if (!moveMode) {
+        return;
+      }
+      if (moveMode.isActive()) {
+        if (moveMode.isGrabbed(row)) {
+          moveMode.commit();
+        }
+        return;
+      }
+      moveMode.tryGrab(row);
+    };
+
+    // Move-mode pointer + column switch, ahead of the element's built-in nav.
+    element.addClickHandler((event) => {
+      if (moveMode?.isActive() && moveMode.handlePointer(event)) {
+        event.preventDefault();
+        return true;
+      }
+      const columnToggle = event.target.closest(COLUMN_TOGGLE);
+      if (columnToggle) {
+        // Let the native checkbox flip (no preventDefault), then persist.
+        handleColumnToggle(columnToggle, columnUpdateUrl, getToken);
+        return true;
+      }
+      return false;
+    });
+
+    element.addKeyHandler((event) => {
+      // While a row is picked up, move mode owns every key, even one landing
+      // on a control — the carried row must keep taking Space/Enter (drop)
+      // and Escape (cancel) regardless of where focus sits.
+      if (moveMode?.isActive()) {
+        if (moveMode.handleKey(event)) {
+          event.preventDefault();
+        }
+        return true;
+      }
+
+      const row = rowOf(event.target);
+      if (!row) {
+        return false;
+      }
+      // Let a focused in-row control (title link, checkbox, operations
+      // button) handle its own keys instead of the row hijacking them.
+      const control = event.target !== row && event.target.closest(INTERACTIVE);
+      if (control && !control.closest('[data-treegrid-toggle]')) {
+        return false;
+      }
+
+      // Space grabs a movable row; if it cannot grab, fall through so the spine
+      // toggles expand on a parent (Space's pre-move-mode role).
+      if (event.key === ' ') {
+        if (moveMode && moveMode.tryGrab(row)) {
+          event.preventDefault();
+          return true;
+        }
+        return false;
+      }
+      if (
+        event.shiftKey &&
+        (event.key === 'ArrowUp' || event.key === 'ArrowDown')
+      ) {
+        if (moveUrl) {
+          rr.reorderSibling(row, event.key === 'ArrowUp' ? 'up' : 'down', {
+            moveUrl,
+            csrfToken,
+            flashClass: REORDER_CONFIG.flashClass,
+            onCommitted: REORDER_CONFIG.onCommitted,
+            titleSelector: REORDER_CONFIG.titleSelector,
+          });
+          event.preventDefault();
+          return true;
+        }
+      }
+      return false;
+    });
+
+    // A pointer press genuinely outside the component cancels an active move
+    // (focus leaving the tree must not — carrying a row blurs it, and searching
+    // moves focus to the search field).
+    const onOutsidePointer = (event) => {
+      if (!moveMode?.isActive() || !(event.target instanceof Node)) {
+        return;
+      }
+      if (container && !container.contains(event.target)) {
+        moveMode.cancel();
+      }
+    };
+    document.addEventListener('mousedown', onOutsidePointer);
+
+    // Search jump-to and dismiss.
+    const jumpHandler = ns.attachJumpClickHandler({ tree, expand, moveMode });
+    const detachSearchPanel = container
+      ? ns.attachSearchPanel(container)
+      : null;
+
+    // Stream the rest of a truncated top level in as the editor scrolls.
+    const detachPaging = ns.attachTopLevelPaging(element);
+
+    // "Keyboard commands" dialog. Closing uses a native <form method="dialog">,
+    // so only opening needs JS; degrades to a no-op without dialog.showModal.
+    const helpToggle = container?.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__help-toggle');
+    const helpDialog = container?.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__help-dialog');
+    let openHelp = null;
+    if (
+      helpToggle &&
+      helpDialog &&
+      typeof helpDialog.showModal === 'function'
+    ) {
+      openHelp = () => helpDialog.showModal();
+      helpToggle.addEventListener('click', openHelp);
+    }
+
+    // Drag needs the CSRF token; defer the controller until it resolves, keeping
+    // the token out of URLs (and access logs). move-mode and the column toggle
+    // read it lazily through getToken().
+    const base = drupalSettings.path?.baseUrl ?? '/';
+    fetch(`${base}session/token`, { credentials: 'same-origin' })
+      .then((response) => response.text())
+      .then((token) => {
+        csrfToken = token;
+      })
+      .catch(() => {
+        csrfToken = undefined;
+      })
+      .finally(() => {
+        if (!moveUrl) {
+          // eslint-disable-next-line no-console
+          console.warn(
+            '[menu-tree] drupalSettings.menuTreeUi.moveUrl missing — drag disabled.',
+          );
+          return;
+        }
+        drag = new rr.DragController(
+          tree,
+          moveUrl,
+          expand,
+          csrfToken,
+          indicator,
+          () => moveMode?.cancel(),
+          (row) => onHandleTap(row),
+          REORDER_CONFIG,
+        );
+        drag.attach();
+        // Reorder is now interactive: the CSRF token has resolved (keyboard and
+        // pointer commits need it) and the drag controller is listening. Tests
+        // wait on this before dispatching a move so they do not race the
+        // deferred wiring.
+        element.dataset.treegridReorderReady = 'true';
+      });
+
+    element.addEventListener(
+      'treegrid:disconnect',
+      () => {
+        moveMode?.cancel();
+        drag?.detach();
+        stickyObserver?.disconnect();
+        document.removeEventListener('mousedown', onOutsidePointer);
+        if (jumpHandler) {
+          document.removeEventListener('click', jumpHandler);
+        }
+        detachSearchPanel?.();
+        detachPaging?.();
+        if (helpToggle && openHelp) {
+          helpToggle.removeEventListener('click', openHelp);
+        }
+        indicator.destroy();
+      },
+      { once: true },
+    );
+  }
+
+  Drupal.behaviors.menuTreeUi = {
+    attach(context) {
+      once(
+        'menu-tree-ui',
+        'drupal-treegrid[data-provider="menu_tree_ui"]',
+        context,
+      ).forEach(wireFeatures);
+    },
+  };
+})(Drupal, drupalSettings, once);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/row-builder.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/row-builder.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..942ee4e19a8e78c12195e7d4ab27aaa9bc4caf63
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/row-builder.js
@@ -0,0 +1,265 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Builds row DOM from the JSON children response.
+ *
+ * NB: Mirrors templates/menu-tree-ui-row.html.twig. If you change one, change
+ * the other — there is no shared template source. Rows are flat <tr role="row">
+ * elements (see js/tree-nav.js); children are inserted as siblings after their
+ * parent, never nested.
+ *
+ * Mirrors the JSON contract MenuTreeController::serializeElement() emits:
+ *   ChildItem: {
+ *     id: string, parent_id: string, title: string, enabled: boolean,
+ *     has_children: boolean, depth: number, url: string, weight: number,
+ *     movable: boolean,
+ *     columns: Object<string, cell>
+ *   }
+ *
+ * Each cell carries a 'type' and is drawn by the treegrid cell renderer
+ * registered for it (see treegrid/js/cells.js). The operations dropbutton is
+ * the last column — a 'markup' cell whose html is pre-rendered server-side with
+ * the active admin theme, injected verbatim, and upgraded by
+ * Drupal.attachBehaviors (see OperationsColumn for why it isn't rebuilt here).
+ *
+ * Registers the menu row renderer as a treegrid provider, and exposes
+ * Drupal.menuTreeUi.buildToggle for the reorder feature's post-move refresh.
+ */
+
+((Drupal) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+  const { setRowLevel } = Drupal.treegrid.treeNav;
+
+  /**
+   * Builds the drag handle for a row.
+   *
+   * The handle is a pointer/drag affordance only: pointer drag arms on it (see
+   * the treegrid_reorder controller's handleSelector) and a click picks the row
+   * up. Keyboard users reorder from the row itself (Space), so the handle is
+   * hidden from assistive technology (aria-hidden) and the row's aria-label
+   * carries the name. The server decides movability via
+   * \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\MenuLinkMovability and sends item.movable; non-movable
+   * rows keep the locked class so the controller skips them. It lives inside
+   * the name cell so it indents with the title (see the row template).
+   *
+   * @param {object} item
+   *   The ChildItem.
+   *
+   * @return {HTMLSpanElement}
+   *   The handle element.
+   */
+  function buildHandle(item) {
+    const handle = document.createElement('span');
+    handle.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
+
+    const icon = document.createElement('span');
+    icon.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__handle-icon';
+
+    if (item.movable) {
+      handle.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__handle';
+      handle.title = Drupal.t('Drag to reorder, or click to pick up');
+    } else {
+      handle.className =
+        'menu-tree-ui-row__handle menu-tree-ui-row__handle--locked';
+      icon.textContent = '·';
+    }
+
+    handle.appendChild(icon);
+    return handle;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Builds the expand/collapse toggle button, or a spacer for leaves.
+   *
+   * @param {object} item
+   *   The ChildItem.
+   *
+   * @return {HTMLElement}
+   *   A button for parents, or a spacer span for leaves.
+   */
+  function buildToggle(item) {
+    if (!item.has_children) {
+      const spacer = document.createElement('span');
+      spacer.className =
+        'menu-tree-ui-row__toggle menu-tree-ui-row__toggle--spacer';
+      spacer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
+      return spacer;
+    }
+    const toggle = document.createElement('button');
+    toggle.type = 'button';
+    toggle.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__toggle';
+    // The generic <drupal-treegrid> element finds the disclosure control by this
+    // hook, so it needs no knowledge of menu CSS classes.
+    toggle.setAttribute('data-treegrid-toggle', '');
+    // Operated from the row (Left/Right/Enter), not via Tab; mouse-clickable.
+    toggle.tabIndex = -1;
+    toggle.setAttribute(
+      'aria-label',
+      Drupal.t('Toggle children of @title', { '@title': item.title }),
+    );
+    const chevron = document.createElement('span');
+    chevron.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
+    chevron.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__chevron';
+    chevron.textContent = '▸';
+    toggle.appendChild(chevron);
+    return toggle;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Builds the name cell — indent wrapper, handle, toggle, and title.
+   *
+   * @param {object} item
+   *   The ChildItem.
+   *
+   * @return {HTMLTableCellElement}
+   *   The name <td>.
+   */
+  function buildNameCell(item) {
+    const cell = document.createElement('td');
+    cell.setAttribute('role', 'gridcell');
+    cell.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__cell menu-tree-ui-row__cell--name';
+
+    const name = document.createElement('div');
+    name.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__name';
+    // The treegrid spine indents this cell (setRowLevel) via this hook.
+    name.dataset.treegridNameCell = '';
+
+    name.appendChild(buildHandle(item));
+    name.appendChild(buildToggle(item));
+
+    // Link the title to the menu link's destination (the classic admin
+    // pattern); route-less links (<nolink> etc.) stay plain text.
+    const title = document.createElement(item.linked ? 'a' : 'span');
+    title.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__title';
+    if (item.linked) {
+      title.href = item.url;
+      // The title link joins the active row's roving tab order.
+      title.dataset.treegridControl = '';
+    }
+    title.textContent = item.title;
+    name.appendChild(title);
+
+    cell.appendChild(name);
+    return cell;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Builds one column cell <td>.
+   *
+   * The widget inside is built by the treegrid cell-renderer registered for
+   * cell.type (see treegrid/js/cells.js). An unregistered type renders an empty
+   * cell, so a new column type does not break an older client.
+   *
+   * @param {string} colId
+   *   The column plugin ID.
+   * @param {object} cell
+   *   The cell data.
+   * @param {string} rowId
+   *   The owning row's link ID.
+   *
+   * @return {HTMLTableCellElement}
+   *   The column <td>.
+   */
+  function buildColumnCell(colId, cell, rowId) {
+    const td = document.createElement('td');
+    td.setAttribute('role', 'gridcell');
+    td.className = 'menu-tree-ui-row__cell menu-tree-ui-row__column';
+    td.dataset.column = colId;
+
+    const widget = Drupal.treegrid.renderCell(cell, { colId, rowId });
+    if (widget) {
+      td.appendChild(widget);
+    }
+
+    return td;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Builds one <tr role="row"> row from a ChildItem.
+   *
+   * @param {object} item
+   *   The ChildItem.
+   * @param {number} depth
+   *   The row's depth (1-based).
+   * @param {number} posInSet
+   *   The 1-based position among siblings.
+   * @param {number} setSize
+   *   The number of siblings.
+   *
+   * @return {HTMLTableRowElement}
+   *   The row element.
+   */
+  function buildRow(item, depth, posInSet, setSize) {
+    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
+    tr.setAttribute('role', 'row');
+    tr.dataset.id = item.id;
+    tr.dataset.parentId = item.parent_id ?? '';
+    tr.dataset.hasChildren = String(item.has_children);
+    tr.dataset.movable = String(item.movable);
+    tr.setAttribute('aria-posinset', String(posInSet));
+    tr.setAttribute('aria-setsize', String(setSize));
+    if (item.has_children) {
+      tr.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
+    }
+    // The row's accessible name: the title, plus "(locked)" when it cannot be
+    // reordered. An explicit name keeps a screen reader from flattening the
+    // in-row controls into one utterance; per-column state is announced by each
+    // cell's control on Tab, so this stays column-agnostic (see the template).
+    tr.setAttribute(
+      'aria-label',
+      item.movable
+        ? item.title
+        : Drupal.t('@title (locked)', { '@title': item.title }),
+    );
+    // Lazy-loaded rows are never the initial tab stop; the active row is set as
+    // the cursor moves (see treeNav.focusRow). aria-selected is added only while
+    // a row is picked up for a move (see move-mode), so it is absent here.
+    tr.setAttribute('tabindex', '-1');
+    tr.className = [
+      'menu-tree-ui-row',
+      item.enabled ? '' : 'menu-tree-ui-row--disabled',
+      item.has_children ? 'menu-tree-ui-row--parent' : 'menu-tree-ui-row--leaf',
+    ]
+      .filter(Boolean)
+      .join(' ');
+
+    tr.appendChild(buildNameCell(item));
+    // aria-level + indent in one place (the name cell now exists in the row).
+    setRowLevel(tr, depth);
+    Object.entries(item.columns).forEach(([colId, cell]) => {
+      tr.appendChild(buildColumnCell(colId, cell, item.id));
+    });
+
+    return tr;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Builds a DocumentFragment of sibling rows from items.
+   *
+   * @param {Array<object>} items
+   *   The ChildItems.
+   * @param {number} depth
+   *   The depth at which to render the rows.
+   *
+   * @return {DocumentFragment}
+   *   The fragment of <tr> rows.
+   */
+  function buildRows(items, depth) {
+    const fragment = document.createDocumentFragment();
+    const setSize = items.length;
+    items.forEach((item, i) => {
+      fragment.appendChild(buildRow(item, depth, i + 1, setSize));
+    });
+    return fragment;
+  }
+
+  // buildToggle is shared so menu-tree.js's applyParentMetadata can rebuild a
+  // row's disclosure toggle after a move refresh without duplicating the markup
+  // (and its translated aria-label). buildRows/buildRow reach the spine through
+  // the registered provider object below, so they need no namespace export.
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi.buildToggle = buildToggle;
+
+  // Register the menu renderer with the generic treegrid element. registerProvider
+  // adopts any <drupal-treegrid data-provider="menu_tree_ui"> already connected
+  // (the treegrid library loads, and the element upgrades, before this runs).
+  Drupal.treegrid.registerProvider('menu_tree_ui', { buildRows, buildRow });
+})(Drupal);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/search.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/search.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..082e911a111a2c3570bbcbb5e4d142a1e3e02762
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/search.js
@@ -0,0 +1,78 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Dismissal behavior for the htmx-driven search results popover.
+ *
+ * htmx swaps results into #menu-tree-ui-search-results on keyup; the popover
+ * self-hides when empty (CSS `:not(:has(*))`). This module empties it - without
+ * touching the typed query - so the popover goes away when the user is done
+ * with it: after selecting a result, on Escape, or on a click outside the
+ * search box. The query text stays so the search can be resumed or refined.
+ *
+ * Exposes Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachSearchPanel.
+ */
+
+((Drupal) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+
+  /**
+   * Wires popover dismissal for one search container.
+   *
+   * @param {HTMLElement} container
+   *   The .menu-tree-ui__search-container (or any ancestor of the input and
+   *   results) to wire.
+   *
+   * @return {function()}
+   *   A teardown function that removes the listeners.
+   */
+  function attachSearchPanel(container) {
+    const input = container.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__search-input');
+    const results = container.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__search-results');
+    if (!input || !results) {
+      return () => {};
+    }
+
+    // Empties the popover (CSS hides an empty popover). Leaves input.value.
+    const clear = () => {
+      results.replaceChildren();
+    };
+
+    // A result link/button was activated. Defer the clear so the click's other
+    // handlers (jump-to.js navigates to the row) read the result first.
+    const onResultsClick = (event) => {
+      if (
+        event.target instanceof Element &&
+        event.target.closest('[data-mtu-jump-id], a')
+      ) {
+        window.setTimeout(clear, 0);
+      }
+    };
+
+    // Escape hides the popover but keeps the query - preventDefault stops the
+    // browser's native "clear the search field" behavior.
+    const onKeyDown = (event) => {
+      if (event.key === 'Escape' && results.firstElementChild) {
+        event.preventDefault();
+        clear();
+      }
+    };
+
+    // A click anywhere outside the search box dismisses the popover.
+    const onDocumentClick = (event) => {
+      if (event.target instanceof Node && !container.contains(event.target)) {
+        clear();
+      }
+    };
+
+    results.addEventListener('click', onResultsClick);
+    input.addEventListener('keydown', onKeyDown);
+    document.addEventListener('click', onDocumentClick);
+
+    return () => {
+      results.removeEventListener('click', onResultsClick);
+      input.removeEventListener('keydown', onKeyDown);
+      document.removeEventListener('click', onDocumentClick);
+    };
+  }
+
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachSearchPanel = attachSearchPanel;
+})(Drupal);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/top-level-paging.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/top-level-paging.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..a299718eafac63403b26d843c4c5d106e75f9955
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/top-level-paging.js
@@ -0,0 +1,137 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Streams the rest of a truncated top level in as the editor scrolls.
+ *
+ * The server renders only the first page of top-level rows (see
+ * MenuTreeUiConstants::TOP_LEVEL_PAGE_SIZE) so a very wide top level does not
+ * make first paint expensive. When the top level was truncated, an
+ * IntersectionObserver sentinel below the tree fetches the next page from the
+ * children endpoint (parent empty, with an offset) and appends the rows as
+ * top-level siblings, until the server reports no more remain.
+ *
+ * Exposes Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachTopLevelPaging.
+ */
+
+((Drupal) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+  const { setRowControlsActive } = Drupal.treegrid.treeNav;
+
+  const ROW = 'tr[role="row"]';
+
+  /**
+   * Wires scroll-triggered paging for a truncated top level.
+   *
+   * @param {HTMLElement} element
+   *   The upgraded <drupal-treegrid> element (element.tree / element.rowWindow
+   *   are set).
+   *
+   * @return {function()}
+   *   A teardown function that stops observing and removes the sentinel.
+   */
+  function attachTopLevelPaging(element) {
+    const total = parseInt(element.dataset.treegridTopTotal, 10) || 0;
+    const pageSize = parseInt(element.dataset.treegridPageSize, 10) || 0;
+    const { childrenUrl } = element.dataset;
+    const { tree } = element;
+    const noop = () => {};
+    if (!tree || !childrenUrl || pageSize <= 0) {
+      return noop;
+    }
+    const tbody = tree.querySelector('tbody');
+    const provider = Drupal.treegrid.providers[element.dataset.provider];
+    if (!tbody || !provider) {
+      return noop;
+    }
+    let offset = tbody.querySelectorAll(`${ROW}[data-parent-id=""]`).length;
+    if (offset >= total) {
+      return noop;
+    }
+
+    let loading = false;
+    let done = false;
+
+    // A sentinel after the table (not a table row, so tree navigation ignores
+    // it); scrolling it into view triggers the next fetch.
+    const sentinel = document.createElement('div');
+    sentinel.className = 'menu-tree-ui__paging-sentinel';
+    sentinel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
+    element.appendChild(sentinel);
+
+    // Reassigned to disconnect the observer once it exists, so teardown()
+    // can be defined (and called from loadNext) before the observer is.
+    let stopObserving = noop;
+
+    /**
+     * Stops paging: disconnect the observer and drop the sentinel.
+     */
+    function teardown() {
+      done = true;
+      stopObserving();
+      sentinel.remove();
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Fetches and appends the next page of top-level rows.
+     *
+     * @return {Promise<void>}
+     *   Resolves once the page is appended (or paging stopped on failure/end).
+     */
+    async function loadNext() {
+      if (loading || done) {
+        return;
+      }
+      loading = true;
+      try {
+        const url = new URL(childrenUrl, window.location.origin);
+        url.searchParams.set('offset', String(offset));
+        const response = await fetch(url.toString(), {
+          headers: { Accept: 'application/json' },
+          credentials: 'same-origin',
+        });
+        if (!response.ok) {
+          teardown();
+          return;
+        }
+        const data = await response.json();
+        const items = data.items ?? [];
+        const fragment = provider.buildRows(items, 1);
+        const built = Array.from(fragment.children);
+        tbody.appendChild(fragment);
+        built.forEach((row, i) => {
+          // buildRows numbers within the page; renumber against the full level
+          // so a screen reader announces "row N of total", not "N of page".
+          row.setAttribute('aria-posinset', String(offset + i + 1));
+          row.setAttribute('aria-setsize', String(total));
+          if (Drupal.attachBehaviors) {
+            Drupal.attachBehaviors(row);
+          }
+          setRowControlsActive(row, false);
+          element.rowWindow?.observe(row);
+        });
+        offset += items.length;
+        if (!data.has_more) {
+          teardown();
+        }
+      } catch (e) {
+        teardown();
+      } finally {
+        loading = false;
+      }
+    }
+
+    const observer = new IntersectionObserver(
+      (entries) => {
+        if (entries.some((entry) => entry.isIntersecting)) {
+          loadNext();
+        }
+      },
+      { root: null, rootMargin: '400px 0px' },
+    );
+    observer.observe(sentinel);
+    stopObserving = () => observer.disconnect();
+
+    return teardown;
+  }
+
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi.attachTopLevelPaging = attachTopLevelPaging;
+})(Drupal);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/working-copy.js b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/working-copy.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..287136b976ae12562a53f177096229973ec607d8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/js/working-copy.js
@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Save / Cancel wiring for the menu tree working copy.
+ *
+ * Moves are recorded in a per-user server-side working copy instead of being
+ * written immediately, so an editor can make many changes and then keep or
+ * discard them. This posts to the save/cancel routes and reveals the "unsaved
+ * changes" notice after the first recorded change.
+ *
+ * It is a Drupal.behaviors attach rather than part of the <drupal-treegrid> custom
+ * element because the action bar lives in the page template, outside the
+ * element. It listens for the menu-tree-ui:changed event the move commit
+ * dispatches, keeping the two decoupled.
+ */
+
+((Drupal, drupalSettings, once) => {
+  Drupal.menuTreeUi = Drupal.menuTreeUi || {};
+
+  let csrfToken;
+
+  // Bound once for the page lifetime (see attach). A per-bar document listener
+  // would accumulate: once() only guards re-wiring the same bar element, so an
+  // htmx swap that injects a new action bar would add another permanent listener
+  // and retain the detached one's closure.
+  let changedListenerBound = false;
+
+  /**
+   * Reveals the unsaved-changes notice when a change is recorded.
+   *
+   * Queries the notice fresh rather than closing over one, so a single listener
+   * serves whatever action bar is currently in the DOM.
+   */
+  function revealUnsavedNotices() {
+    document
+      .querySelectorAll('.menu-tree-ui__unsaved')
+      .forEach((notice) => notice.classList.remove('js-hide'));
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Fetches (and caches) the CSRF token for the working-copy POSTs.
+   *
+   * @return {Promise<string>}
+   *   The token, or '' when it could not be fetched.
+   */
+  async function getToken() {
+    if (csrfToken !== undefined) {
+      return csrfToken;
+    }
+    const base = drupalSettings.path?.baseUrl ?? '/';
+    try {
+      const response = await fetch(`${base}session/token`, {
+        credentials: 'same-origin',
+      });
+      if (!response.ok) {
+        // Don't cache a failure: an error page body would otherwise become the
+        // "token" forever. Leave csrfToken undefined so the next Save/Cancel
+        // retries the fetch.
+        return '';
+      }
+      csrfToken = await response.text();
+    } catch (e) {
+      return '';
+    }
+    return csrfToken;
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * POSTs to a working-copy endpoint with the CSRF header.
+   *
+   * @param {string} url
+   *   The save or cancel URL.
+   *
+   * @return {Promise<object>}
+   *   The decoded JSON response, or an error-shaped object.
+   */
+  async function post(url) {
+    const token = await getToken();
+    try {
+      const response = await fetch(url, {
+        method: 'POST',
+        headers: { Accept: 'application/json', 'X-CSRF-Token': token ?? '' },
+        credentials: 'same-origin',
+      });
+      return await response.json().catch(() => ({ ok: false }));
+    } catch (e) {
+      return { ok: false };
+    }
+  }
+
+  /**
+   * Wires one action bar's Save / Cancel buttons and unsaved notice.
+   *
+   * @param {HTMLElement} bar
+   *   The .menu-tree-ui__actions element.
+   */
+  function setupActions(bar) {
+    const settings = drupalSettings.menuTreeUi ?? {};
+    // The unsaved notice sits in the action bar beside these buttons; scope the
+    // lookup to the whole region so it is found wherever in the bar it renders.
+    const notice = bar
+      .closest('.menu-tree-ui')
+      ?.querySelector('.menu-tree-ui__unsaved');
+    const save = bar.querySelector('[data-mtu-action="save"]');
+    const cancel = bar.querySelector('[data-mtu-action="cancel"]');
+
+    save?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
+      if (!settings.saveUrl) {
+        return;
+      }
+      const result = await post(settings.saveUrl);
+      if (result.ok) {
+        // The tree already shows the saved order (it was rendering the working
+        // copy, which is now committed), so there is nothing to re-fetch. Don't
+        // reload — that would collapse every expanded section and lose scroll
+        // position on large menus. Just retire the unsaved notice.
+        notice?.classList.add('js-hide');
+        Drupal.treegrid.announce(Drupal.t('Changes saved.'), 'polite');
+      } else {
+        Drupal.treegrid.announce(
+          result.message ?? Drupal.t('Save failed.'),
+          'assertive',
+        );
+      }
+    });
+
+    cancel?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
+      if (!settings.cancelUrl) {
+        return;
+      }
+      const result = await post(settings.cancelUrl);
+      if (result.ok) {
+        window.location.reload();
+      } else {
+        Drupal.treegrid.announce(
+          result.message ?? Drupal.t('Cancel failed.'),
+          'assertive',
+        );
+      }
+    });
+  }
+
+  Drupal.behaviors.menuTreeUiWorkingCopy = {
+    attach(context) {
+      if (!changedListenerBound) {
+        document.addEventListener('menu-tree-ui:changed', revealUnsavedNotices);
+        changedListenerBound = true;
+      }
+      once('mtu-working-copy', '.menu-tree-ui__actions', context).forEach(
+        setupActions,
+      );
+    },
+  };
+})(Drupal, drupalSettings, once);
diff --git a/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/menu_tree_ui.api.php b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/menu_tree_ui.api.php
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9cc029a35ada2bde3a934c1e15f61d7cf7dfeae2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/modules/menu_tree_ui/menu_tree_ui.api.php
@@ -0,0 +1,176 @@
+<?php
+
+/**
+ * @file
+ * Hooks provided by the Menu tree UI module.
+ */
+
+use Drupal\Core\Menu\MenuLinkTreeElement;
+
+/**
+ * @addtogroup hooks
+ * @{
+ */
+
+/**
+ * Alters a single loaded level of a menu tree.
+ *
+ * Fires at the end of \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeLoader::loadLevel(),
+ * once per level fetched — the initial page load and every lazy "expand" fetch
+ * call it separately, each time with only that level's elements. Implement
+ * this to add, remove, or reorder tree elements at a level, or to react to
+ * which level was requested.
+ *
+ * @param \Drupal\Core\Menu\MenuLinkTreeElement[] &$elements
+ *   The level's tree elements, access-checked and sorted by weight.
+ * @param string $menu_name
+ *   Menu entity ID (e.g. 'main', 'admin').
+ * @param string|null $parent_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the parent whose children were loaded, or NULL for the menu's
+ *   top level.
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeLoader::loadLevel()
+ */
+function hook_menu_tree_ui_level_alter(array &$elements, string $menu_name, ?string $parent_id) {
+  // Hide a specific link from the tree UI without removing it from the menu.
+  foreach ($elements as $key => $element) {
+    if ($element->link->getPluginId() === 'my_module.hidden_link') {
+      unset($elements[$key]);
+    }
+  }
+}
+
+/**
+ * Alters the merged results of a menu tree search.
+ *
+ * Fires at the end of \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeLoader::search(),
+ * after results from all tagged menu_tree_ui.search_provider services have
+ * been merged, deduplicated by link plugin ID, and sliced to the requested
+ * limit. Implement this to add, remove, or reorder search results.
+ *
+ * Each result item is an array with keys 'id' (the link's plugin ID), 'title',
+ * 'enabled' (bool), 'edit_url' (string or NULL), 'breadcrumb' (string[] of
+ * display titles from the menu root down to the result), and
+ * 'breadcrumb_ids' (string[] of the matching plugin IDs).
+ *
+ * @param array &$results
+ *   The merged, deduplicated, limit-sliced result list.
+ * @param string $menu_name
+ *   Menu entity ID being searched.
+ * @param string $query
+ *   The search string, already trimmed.
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeLoader::search()
+ */
+function hook_menu_tree_ui_search_results_alter(array &$results, string $menu_name, string $query) {
+  // Drop results the current user is not allowed to see for some
+  // module-specific reason not already covered by the tree's access check.
+  foreach ($results as $key => $result) {
+    if (str_starts_with($result['id'], 'my_module.restricted:')) {
+      unset($results[$key]);
+    }
+  }
+}
+
+/**
+ * Alters a menu link row's operations (Edit, Delete, Add child, …).
+ *
+ * Fires from \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Plugin\TreegridColumn\OperationsColumn for
+ * every row that has at least one operation. The operations array has the
+ * same shape as hook_entity_operation(): keyed by machine-readable operation
+ * ID, each entry has 'title', 'url', and 'weight'.
+ *
+ * @param array $operations
+ *   Operations keyed by ID; each has 'title' (translatable string), 'url'
+ *   (a \Drupal\Core\Url), and 'weight' (int).
+ * @param \Drupal\Core\Menu\MenuLinkTreeElement $element
+ *   The tree element the row represents.
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Plugin\TreegridColumn\OperationsColumn
+ */
+function hook_menu_tree_ui_row_operations_alter(array &$operations, MenuLinkTreeElement $element) {
+  // Add a custom operation to every row.
+  $operations['my_module_action'] = [
+    'title' => t('Do something'),
+    'url' => \Drupal\Core\Url::fromRoute('my_module.do_something', [
+      'menu_link' => $element->link->getPluginId(),
+    ]),
+    'weight' => 50,
+  ];
+}
+
+/**
+ * Vetoes a menu link move before menu_tree_ui's own checks run.
+ *
+ * Fires from \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeMover::validateConstraints(),
+ * after \Drupal\treegrid_reorder\TreeReorderManager's universal self-target and
+ * cycle checks pass, but before menu_tree_ui checks whether the link is
+ * movable, belongs to the target menu, or fits the 9-level depth cap. This
+ * runs on every validation, including the record-time check made as the
+ * editor drags or keyboard-moves a row, and the re-validation made when the
+ * working copy is committed on Save.
+ *
+ * To block the move, set $veto['veto'] = TRUE. Set $veto['message'] to a
+ * translated string to give the editor a specific reason; otherwise a generic
+ * "Move blocked by a module." message is shown.
+ *
+ * @param array $veto
+ *   Empty on entry. Set $veto['veto'] = TRUE to block the move, and
+ *   optionally $veto['message'] with a user-facing reason.
+ * @param string $menu_name
+ *   The menu the move is happening within.
+ * @param string $moved_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the link being moved.
+ * @param string $new_parent_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the prospective new parent, or empty string for the menu
+ *   root.
+ * @param string|null $before_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the sibling the moved link would sit before, or NULL to drop
+ *   at the end.
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeMover::validateConstraints()
+ * @see hook_menu_tree_ui_post_move()
+ */
+function hook_menu_tree_ui_pre_move_alter(array &$veto, string $menu_name, string $moved_id, string $new_parent_id, ?string $before_id) {
+  // Prevent moving a protected link out of the menu root.
+  if ($moved_id === 'my_module.protected_link' && $new_parent_id !== '') {
+    $veto['veto'] = TRUE;
+    $veto['message'] = t('This link must stay at the top level.');
+  }
+}
+
+/**
+ * Reacts to a menu link move that has just been written to storage.
+ *
+ * Fires from \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeMover::applyMove(), once the
+ * move has been persisted through the menu link manager (and destination
+ * siblings renumbered). Implementations receive the final weight the moved
+ * link was given; the parent is $new_parent_id, exactly as validated.
+ *
+ * @param string $menu_name
+ *   The menu the move happened within.
+ * @param string $moved_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the link that was moved.
+ * @param string $new_parent_id
+ *   Plugin ID of the new parent, or empty string for the menu root.
+ * @param int $weight
+ *   The weight the moved link was given among its new siblings.
+ *
+ * @see \Drupal\menu_tree_ui\Service\MenuTreeMover::applyMove()
+ * @see hook_menu_tree_ui_pre_move_alter()
+ */
+function hook_menu_tree_ui_post_move(string $menu_name, string $moved_id, string $new_parent_id, int $weight) {
+  // Log moves of a specific link for an audit trail.
+  if ($moved_id === 'my_module.audited_link') {
+    \Drupal::logger('my_module')->info('Link %id moved to parent %parent at weight %weight in menu %menu.', [
+      '%id' => $moved_id,
+      '%parent' => $new_parent_id,
+      '%weight' => $weight,
+      '%menu' => $menu_name,
+    ]);
+  }
+}
+
+/**
+ * @} End of "addtogroup hooks".
+ */
